This is what I think is happening (though I might be wrong)...

Before the wizard, you think that you have plently of time to make each
move.  After the wizard, you think that you need to get out of the
dungeon as quickly as possible, which includes making moves faster than
you would have before the wizard.

After the wizard, you can still take a large amount of time to make
each move.  Also, it is better to cautiously take extra turns, than to
recklessly ascend in the fewest number of possible turns.



